7. Frequentist Regret

7.1 Linear UCB Inside the Conformal Set

We replace the inner Thompson sampling step by a linear UCB (OFUL-style) confidence set restricted to \mathcal{C}_t. The confidence ellipsoid is

\Theta_t = \left\{\theta \in \mathbb{R}^d : \|\theta - \hat{\theta}_t\|_{V_t} \le \sqrt{\beta_t}\right\},

where V_t = \lambda I + \sum_{s=1}^t x_s x_s^\top and \beta_t is the OFUL radius.

7.2 Regret Bound

Theorem 5 (Frequentist Regret). Under Assumptions 2–7, the linear UCB policy restricted to the conformal set achieves

\mathbb{E}[R_T] \le \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d\sqrt{T}) + O(\sqrt{T}),

where the first term is the minimax-optimal linear bandit rate and the second term is the conformal overhead.

Proof. The OFUL analysis of Abbasi-Yadkori et al. (2011) yields \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d\sqrt{T}) for the unrestricted policy. The conformal restriction \mathcal{C}_t \subseteq \mathcal{A} can only remove arms, so the restricted regret is bounded by the unrestricted regret plus the out-of-set conformal overhead. Under the decaying ACI step size, the overhead is O(\sqrt{T}) (Corollary 3). \square

Remark 5. The bound \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d\sqrt{T}) + O(\sqrt{T}) is minimax-optimal up to logarithmic factors when d \to \infty, since the conformal overhead is asymptotically dominated by the leading term. When d is fixed, the O(\sqrt{T}) overhead may be the dominant term; in this regime, the bound is not strictly minimax-optimal but remains sublinear.

Remark 6. This improves the \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d^{3/2}\sqrt{T}) rate of linear Thompson sampling (Agrawal & Goyal, 2013) to the minimax-optimal \widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(d\sqrt{T}).

