Appendix H: Complexity Analysis

H.1 Per-Iteration Complexity

Operation Complexity
Forward pass V_\theta O(p)
Forward pass \pi_\phi O(q)
Belief encoder O(d_{\mathrm{enc}})
Conformal quantile (sorted window) O(n\log n)
Action selection (argmax over \mathcal{C}_t) O(K)
Total O(p+q+d_{\mathrm{enc}}+n\log n+K)

H.2 Memory Complexity

O(p+q+d_{\mathrm{enc}}+n)

for network parameters and the calibration window.

H.3 Sample Complexity

Under the assumptions of the convergence analysis, the number of iterations to achieve \varepsilon-accuracy in the value function is

T_\varepsilon=O\left(\frac{1}{(1-\gamma)^2\varepsilon^2}\log\frac{1}{\delta}\right),

where \delta is the confidence parameter. This matches the standard sample complexity of approximate value iteration with function approximation.

