Appendix I: Summary of Corrections to the Original Formulation

Item Original Corrected
Perov extension Presented as necessary for non-strict depletion Removed; unnecessary under compact \mathcal{R} (Theorem 1 covers all cases)
Bayesian regret \sqrt{2K\sigma^2H(A^\star)T}+\alpha T+O(\sqrt{T}) \sqrt{2K\sigma^2H(A^\star)T}+O(\sqrt{T}) with decaying ACI step size
Information-ratio restriction Asserted without proof Justified via Lemma D.1 with explicit O(1/\sqrt{t}) decay of out-of-set regret
Two-time-scale boundedness Not stated Explicit boundedness assumption (Assumption F.2) and compact parameter spaces (Assumption F.1)
Expectation operator P(ds\mid m) (undefined) b(ds) (belief-based, with memory sufficiency Assumption 1)
Safety proof Cited complementary slackness alone Cites saddle-point property (Theorem G.1) for primal feasibility
ACI step size Constant \gamma_{\mathrm{ACI}} Decaying \gamma_{\mathrm{ACI},t}=\gamma_0/\sqrt{t}
Action selection \arg\min, +\infty for infeasible \arg\max, -\infty for infeasible
Dual update sign [\lambda_t-\eta(\text{cost}-\rho_0)]_+ [\lambda_t+\eta(\text{cost}-\rho_0)]_+
Dual problem \max_\lambda\min_\phi \min_\lambda\max_\phi

These corrections preserve the conceptual framework while making the theoretical guarantees rigorous and the algorithm internally consistent. The highest-impact improvements are the removal of the unnecessary Perov apparatus under compact resources, the correction of the Bayesian regret bound to restore sublinearity, the explicit justification of the information-ratio restriction, and the addition of the required boundedness assumption for the two-time-scale convergence.

